            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A contactless patient monitoring system (10) includes a first imager (12) configured to capture first image data (14) of a target area (16) within a first field of view (18). A second imager (20) is operably coupled to the first imager (12). The second imager (20) is configured to capture second image data (22) of the target area (16) within a second field of view (24). An emitter (26) is operably coupled to at least one of the first imager (12) and the second imager (20). The emitter (26) is configured to emit light (28) within a predetermined wavelength range. A controller (30) is communicatively coupled to the first imager (12), the second imager (20), and the emitter (26). The controller (30) is configured to determine a facial region (32) of a person in the first image data (14), determine a region of interest (34) in the second image data (22) that coincides with the facial region (32) in the first image data (14), and determine a coordinate (X, Y) of a head position (36) within the facial region (32).</p>
            </abstract>
